  "hypothesis_and_conclusion_maps": {
    "common": "Actual law preservation plus measurable intertwining, not Gaussian moment matching alone.",
    "pbps": "nu=mu.prod gamma with arbitrary mu held fixed. S reflects only Gaussian noise. Phi supplies literal Y=X+sqrt(eta)Z; R reflects augmented second coordinate about first. Involutivity is separately calculated.",
    "concentration": "nu=gamma.prod gamma with both centered identical Gaussian copies, Phi=id and R=S=Ttheta. This preserves the coordinate-law integral, permitting the authored conditional Stein calculation.",
    "failure_boundary": "At theta=pi/2, Ttheta maps mu.prod gamma to gamma.prod((-id)#mu). Unless mu=gamma (and its negation has the required law), arbitrary mu fails rotation preservation. Reflection is involutive, but generic rotation is not. Identically distributed centered anisotropic copies still have product rotation invariance; covariance scale must be calibrated separately for concentration constants. Neither law invariant identity implies a process, nonexplosion, convergence, algorithmic cost, theorem equivalence or certified functor."
  },
  "source_reuse_provenance": "All9 pinned inputs have identical raw/LF bytes to the original independent source/mathematical review. Reused that direct PBPS/SHPHMC primary balanced-span reading and exact public/API review; this successor checks the exact correction, full metadata preservation and canonical RAW discovery. No new blind primary preread is claimed.",
  "math_detail": {
    "common_pushforward": "R#(Phi#nu)=(R o Phi)#nu=(Phi o S)#nu=Phi#(S#nu)=Phi#nu for actual measurable maps with the stated exact law identity.",
    "pbps_fixed_arbitrary_mu": "S(x,z)=(x,-z) fixes arbitrary probability mu. Gamma negation symmetry and product-map identity preserve mu.prod gamma. R o Phi=Phi o S holds exactly for the literal generative Y=X+sqrt(eta)Z; R involutivity is separate.",
    "gaussian_rotation": "Ttheta uses identical centered Gaussian copies. The pinned Fernique API permits anisotropic Gaussian covariance; preservation of law is stronger data than covariance agreement alone for non-Gaussian distributions. At pi/2, arbitrary mu.prod gamma becomes gamma.prod((-id)#mu), generally a different law.",
    "covariance_calibration": "Law invariance alone says nothing about the required metric/Lipschitz concentration constant. Actual standard Gaussian has covarianceId and uses the separately proved concentration background. Anisotropic centered covariance can retain rotation symmetry; numerical constants require separate covariance-scale analysis.",
    "source_proof_distinction": "PBPS source prints reflection symmetry and generative formula but attributes reflection proof directly to density2.6. Existing ASTIS public generative proof is an explicit extension to arbitrary probability mu/all positive eta, not a density-adapter or paper-wide process theorem. SPHMC prints4.3 and invokes standard Gaussian concentration; ASTIS rotation/Stein/Herbst supplies omitted background and is not attributed to its authors."
  },
